# Frontend State (MobX)

## Store Categories

- `stores/domain/` — Business entities and API actions (`SpecStore`, `GraphStore`).
- `stores/session/` — Auth and user profile (`AuthStore`).
- `stores/ui/` — Transient UI state, computed domain transformations (`UILayoutStore`).

All stores provided via `RootStore` pattern + React Context.

## Rules

- Call `makeObservable(this)` in the constructor.
- Use decorators: `@observable accessor`, `@computed`, `@action`, `@action.bound`.
- `enforceActions: 'always'` — all state mutations must occur inside `@action` methods.
- Async actions: use `runInAction` for state updates after `await`.
- Simple UI state (hover, open/close, form inputs) stays as local `useState`.

## Example

```typescript
import { makeObservable, observable, action, computed, runInAction } from 'mobx';
import type { Spec } from '@kg/shared';
import type { RootStore } from '../root.store.js';

export class SpecStore {
  @observable accessor specs: Spec[] = [];
  @observable accessor loading = false;

  constructor(private readonly rootStore: RootStore) {
    makeObservable(this);
  }

  @computed get publishedSpecs(): Spec[] {
    return this.specs.filter((s) => s.status === 'published');
  }

  @action.bound async loadSpecs(): Promise<void> {
    this.loading = true;
    try {
      const result = await specService.getAll();
      runInAction(() => { this.specs = result; });
    } finally {
      runInAction(() => { this.loading = false; });
    }
  }
}
```

## Anti-patterns

- Mutating state outside an `@action` method.
- Importing stores directly in leaf components — pass data via props.
- Using `makeAutoObservable` — prefer explicit decorators for clarity.
